   00004| // Issue #386: a known-facts inventory query is recognised by composing meaning
   00005| // roles, not by matching raw words per language. The universal algorithm is
   00006| // identical for every language: the prompt either names the knowledge `fact`
   00007| // noun together with an enumerating interrogative and a second-person
   00008| // attribution of knowing, or it matches one of the complete standalone
   00009| // phrasings that ask what the assistant knows even without the noun. The
   00010| // prompt is re-normalised first so the boundary-aware matcher sees punctuation
   00011| // collapsed to spaces. Mirror of is_known_fact_query in
   00012| // src/solver_handlers/self_awareness.rs.
   00013| function isKnownFactQuery(normalized) {
